/// Specifies the Amazon S3 object key name to filter on. An object key name
/// is the name assigned to an object in your Amazon S3 bucket. You specify
/// whether to filter on the suffix or prefix of the object key name. A
/// prefix is a specific string of characters at the beginning of an object
/// key name, which you can use to organize objects. For example, you can
/// start the key names of related objects with a prefix, such as 2023- or
/// engineering/ . Then, you can use FilterRule to find objects in a bucket
/// with key names that have the same prefix. A suffix is similar to a
/// prefix, but it is at the end of the object key name instead of at the
/// beginning.
